 years, 25.5% over 5 years and 4.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 34%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (10.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 34, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 148.6% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 6.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 89%.","It returns 6.4% a year to shareholders (1.8% in buybacks and 4.6% in dividends).","It pays out 200% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 78 employees, each generates about $9.4M of revenue, 4.1x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 10.9% a year.","That works out to $943K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.7M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $113K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":54,"head":"Avoid: operating income covers interest only 0.8x.","pros":["Trades 51% below fair value of $14.30","FCF margin 10.1%","Revenue grew 25.5%/yr over 5y","EV/EBITDA 11.2x vs sector 16.3x","P/FCF 11.5x vs sector 17.8x"],"cons":["ROIC 2.5% vs WACC 7.4%","Net debt/EBITDA 6.3x","Interest coverage only 0.8x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","Piotroski F-score 3/9"],"flags":["Operating income covers interest only 0.8x"],"need":[],"buy_below":12.16,"vc":{"base":14.3,"base_src":"dcf","bear":6.72,"bull":26.17,"alt_median":0.45,"n_alt":1,"gap":30.9885,"dispersion":0.9394,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (94% dispersion)","DCF is 3099% above the other models' median ($0.45)","bull case is 3.9x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.041